//           Scotland, Wales, Northern Ireland) and wherever a country has two places of the same
//           name; '' otherwise.
//   lat/lon degrees (north/east positive), rounded to 0.01 (stored in hundredths, divided on import).
//   tzIndex index into TZS.
//   pop     population in THOUSANDS, rounded (Natural Earth's POP_MAX, the metropolitan figure where
//           it has one; 0 = under 500). Rows are sorted by population, largest first, so a lower
//           index means a bigger place.
//
// Regenerate (sources unpacked anywhere; see ReferenceFiles/orrery-sky/):
//   node ReferenceFiles/orrery-sky/gen-cities.mjs <ne_10m_populated_places.dbf> <tzdata dir> \
